Package: CovDecayAnalyzer
Type: Package
Title: Coverage Decay Analysis Around Viral Genome Anchor Positions
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Olivia", "Daigle", role = "aut"),
    person("Noelle", "Kosarek", role = "aut"),
    person("Carly", "Bobak",
           email = "Carly.A.Bobak@dartmouth.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Tools for quantifying sequencing coverage decay around anchor
    positions in viral genomes, developed for Human Cytomegalovirus (HCMV)
    analyses of coverage around the lytic origin of replication (OriLyt) and
    at genome start and end positions. Given per-base coverage output from
    breseq, the package bins and median-normalizes coverage per sample,
    fits log-linear decay slopes with distance from a user-supplied anchor,
    compares slopes across treatment groups by ANOVA, Kruskal-Wallis, or
    pairwise permutation, and evaluates the significance of the observed
    result against a null distribution built from random genomic anchor
    positions. A viral reads-per-million (RPM) summary is also included.
